{
  "summary": "A DARK KEYNOTE / PRODUCT-PROOF DECK SYSTEM at 16:9 (1600x900 slides), designed as REPEATABLE layouts. GROUND: TRUE black #050607 (not near-black) on every slide, which is the enabling choice — it is dark enough that a single accent glow reads as emitted light. GLOW: exactly ONE emerald #35e0a0 RADIAL glow entering from an EDGE (e.g. radial-gradient at 100% 45% from rgba(45,225,150,.5) to transparent) so it reads as a light source, not a fill; it repeats, dimmed, on the other slides for continuity. GRAIN: a faint film-grain overlay (~6%, SVG feTurbulence) on every slide. COLOR: strictly true-black + white #eef2f0 + ONE emerald #35e0a0 — no second color. TYPE SYSTEM: the hero is ARCHIVO BLACK (a heavy grotesque; Inter Black / Manrope ExtraBold fallback) in white at large scale (~200-260px), tight leading (~.92); ALL metadata/labels are MONOSPACE (SF Mono / JetBrains Mono) in emerald or a muted green-grey; body lines are a clean muted sans. SIGNATURE DEVICES: (a) an INVERTED WHITE PILL as the primary CTA (white ground, black text, fully rounded); (b) a PRODUCT-PROOF mock — a self-built UI rendered in BROWSER CHROME (a window bar with three dots + a fake domain, then KPI tiles) where accent numbers are emerald, so the product demonstrates itself; (c) an OVER-SPECIFIED metric (e.g. '66.0879%') that implies live instrumentation. THREE LAYOUTS: (1) COVER = mono eyebrow + heavy-sans headline anchored bottom-left + white pill CTA; (2) PRODUCT-PROOF = the browser-chrome UI mock centered with KPI tiles + a caption ('the medium is the demo'); (3) METRIC = one huge over-specified number with the emerald spike on the number + one explanatory line. Invent generic copy (e.g. 'Signals, not noise', 'app.r3xdec.design') — never a template brand.",
  "style": {
    "description": "Dark product keynote where light is the color and the product proves itself. A TRUE-black #050607 ground is the enabling move: it is dark enough that ONE emerald #35e0a0 radial glow entering from an edge reads as emitted light rather than a fill. The palette is absolute — black + white + one emerald, nothing else — and a faint grain unifies the surface. Metadata is monospace (the 'instrumented' tell), the primary action is an inverted white pill, and the hero is a heavy grotesque (Archivo Black) in white. The signature is a self-built product-proof mock in browser chrome that demonstrates the product instead of describing it, plus an over-specified metric that implies live data. Confident, technical, modern SaaS/keynote — restrained to one light source and one accent.",
    "prompt": "Design a DARK KEYNOTE / PRODUCT-PROOF DECK SYSTEM at 16:9 as repeatable layouts. Ground: TRUE black #050607 on every slide (not near-black). Add exactly ONE emerald #35e0a0 RADIAL glow entering from an edge (radial-gradient ~100% 45%, rgba(45,225,150,.5) to transparent) so it reads as emitted light; repeat it dimmed on other slides. Lay a faint film-grain overlay (~6%, SVG feTurbulence) over every slide. Palette: strictly true-black + white #eef2f0 + ONE emerald — no second color. Hero: Archivo Black (heavy grotesque; Inter Black/Manrope fallback), white, ~200-260px, line-height ~.92. Metadata/labels: MONOSPACE (SF Mono/JetBrains) in emerald or muted green-grey. Primary CTA: an INVERTED WHITE PILL (white ground, black text, fully rounded). Build three layouts: a COVER (mono eyebrow + heavy-sans headline bottom-left + white pill), a PRODUCT-PROOF slide (a self-built UI mock in BROWSER CHROME — window bar with three dots + a fake domain, then three KPI tiles with emerald accent numbers — plus a caption), and a METRIC slide (one over-specified number like '66.0879%' with the emerald spike on the number). Invent generic copy; never a real template brand."
  },
  "layout_and_structure": {
    "description": "A 16:9 deck of three repeatable layouts on a true-black ground, unified by one emerald edge-glow (dimmed on non-cover slides), monospace metadata, and a faint grain. COVER: a mono eyebrow top-left, a heavy-sans headline anchored bottom-left, an inverted white pill CTA beneath it. PRODUCT-PROOF: a self-built UI mock centered in browser chrome (window bar with three dots + fake domain, then a row of three KPI tiles with emerald accent numbers) over a small muted caption. METRIC: one huge over-specified number centered-left with the emerald spike on the number, and a single explanatory line beneath in muted green-grey. The glow direction and the mono metadata stay constant so the system reads as one deck.",
    "prompts": [
      {
        "part": "Ground, edge-glow, grain, and mono metadata",
        "prompt": "Fill every slide with TRUE black #050607. Add exactly ONE emerald #35e0a0 radial glow entering from the right edge (radial-gradient at ~100% 45%, from rgba(45,225,150,.5) through rgba(45,225,150,.12) to transparent) so it reads as emitted light; on non-cover slides keep it but dim it (~60%). Lay a faint film-grain overlay (~6%, SVG feTurbulence) over each slide. Set all metadata/labels in MONOSPACE (SF Mono/JetBrains Mono) — emerald for the eyebrow, muted green-grey for captions — and a small mono slide-label bottom-right."
      },
      {
        "part": "Cover — heavy headline + inverted pill",
        "prompt": "On the cover, put a monospace eyebrow ('KEYNOTE 2026') top-left in emerald, then anchor a heavy-sans headline to the bottom-left in Archivo Black (Inter Black fallback), white, ~200-260px, line-height ~.92 ('Signals, / not noise'). Beneath it, an INVERTED WHITE PILL CTA (white ground, black text, fully rounded, ~32px/64px padding) reading 'See the demo ->'."
      },
      {
        "part": "Product-proof — self-built UI mock in browser chrome",
        "prompt": "Center a self-built UI mock in BROWSER CHROME: a dark window (#0f1512, 1px #1e2a24 border, ~32px radius) with a title bar carrying three grey dots + a fake domain in mono ('app.r3xdec.design'), then a body of three KPI tiles (each a darker card with a mono uppercase label and a heavy-sans value; the accent values — active users, latency — in emerald). Under it, a small muted caption: 'the product demonstrating itself — the medium is the demo.'"
      },
      {
        "part": "Metric — one over-specified number",
        "prompt": "Center-left, set ONE huge metric in Archivo Black at ~250px with the emerald spike on the number itself ('66.0879%' — deliberately over-specified so it implies live instrumentation), then a single explanatory line beneath in muted green-grey at ~45px, max-width ~72%. One number per slide."
      }
    ]
  },
  "special_ui_components": [
    {
      "component": "Emerald edge-radial glow as emitted light",
      "description": "The single accent, delivered as one radial glow entering from an edge on a true-black ground so it reads as a light source, not a fill.",
      "prompt": "On a TRUE-black #050607 ground, add exactly ONE emerald #35e0a0 radial glow entering from one edge (radial-gradient ~100% 45%, rgba(45,225,150,.5) -> rgba(45,225,150,.12) -> transparent). Keep it on ONE edge so it reads as emitted light; a centered or full-bleed glow stops reading as light. Dim it (~60%) on non-cover slides for continuity. Add no second color anywhere."
    },
    {
      "component": "Product-proof UI mock in browser chrome",
      "description": "A self-built product UI rendered inside a browser window (three dots + fake domain + KPI tiles) that demonstrates the product instead of describing it.",
      "prompt": "Build a self-built UI mock in BROWSER CHROME: a dark window with a title bar (three grey dots + a fake domain in mono) and a body of three KPI tiles (mono uppercase label + heavy-sans value; accent values in emerald). It must look like the real product running, with a caption framing it as the demo ('the medium is the demo'). This is the signature move — prove, don't claim."
    },
    {
      "component": "Inverted white pill CTA",
      "description": "The one bright element: a fully-rounded white pill with black text as the primary action on a dark deck.",
      "prompt": "Style the primary CTA as an INVERTED WHITE PILL: white #eef2f0 ground, black #050607 text, weight 700, fully rounded (border-radius ~100px), generous padding. On a true-black deck it is the single brightest object, so it unambiguously reads as 'the primary action.' Use it once per relevant slide, never twice."
    },
    {
      "component": "Over-specified metric",
      "description": "A deliberately precise number (e.g. 66.0879%) with the accent on the number, implying live instrumentation.",
      "prompt": "Set one hero metric in the heavy grotesque with the emerald spike on the number, and make it OVER-specified (e.g. '66.0879%', '99.98%', '42ms') rather than rounded — the extra digits imply live instrumentation and read as more real than a tidy number. One metric per slide, with a single explanatory line beneath."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "A MINIMAL SWISS / INTERNATIONAL-STYLE DECK SYSTEM at 16:9 (1600x900 slides), designed as REPEATABLE layouts whose entire personality is restraint. GROUND: cool paper #e9ecee on every slide. COLOR: strictly cool paper + near-black ink #16191c + ONE ultramarine #1c39c4 — used as a SPIKE (a few emphasized words, agenda numbers, the italic closer word), never as a fill or a block. THE GOVERNING RULE: emphasis comes from WEIGHT + COLOR, never from SIZE — the deck runs at a near-uniform type size and meaning is carried by a bolder weight (e.g. Public Sans 800 on one word) plus the ultramarine spike; do not solve hierarchy by making things bigger. LAYOUT DISCIPLINE: content is held in a wide LEFT column (max-width ~88%) with a large empty right/bottom margin, flush-left; a single HAIRLINE RULE (1px) is the ONLY ornament anywhere. FURNITURE: a small MONOSPACE rail pinned top-left ('FIELD NOTES · 2026') and a small mono slide-label bottom-right, constant on every slide. TYPE SYSTEM: a clean grotesque (Public Sans; Inter/Helvetica Neue fallback) for headline + agenda at a calm size with selective weight; the CLOSER shifts register to PLAYFAIR DISPLAY (a serif) for one human line. THREE LAYOUTS: (1) COVER = mono rail + a short hairline rule + a headline where one word is bold + ultramarine ('Designing for calm, at scale.'); (2) NUMBERED AGENDA = 01-04 in tabular-nums ultramarine with each row separated by a hairline rule; (3) CLOSER = a single Playfair Display line with the italic ultramarine spike over a monospace cite. Invent generic copy — never a template brand.",
  "style": {
    "description": "International Typographic (Swiss) style: quiet, objective, guided by grid and negative space rather than ornament. Cool paper #e9ecee ground, near-black ink, and ONE ultramarine #1c39c4 spike as the only accent. The governing rule is that emphasis comes from weight and color, never size — one calm size across the deck, with a bolder weight and a few ultramarine words carrying meaning. Content is held in a wide left column with a large empty margin, flush-left; a single hairline rule is the only ornament. A monospace rail and slide-label are the constant furniture; a Playfair Display closer is the one register shift that lets a grotesque deck end on a human note. Considered, restrained, confident in its whitespace — the negative space does as much work as the type.",
    "prompt": "Design a MINIMAL SWISS / INTERNATIONAL-STYLE DECK SYSTEM at 16:9 as repeatable layouts. Ground: cool paper #e9ecee on every slide. Color: cool paper + near-black ink #16191c + ONE ultramarine #1c39c4, used as a SPIKE (a few words, agenda numbers, the closer word) — never a fill or block. GOVERNING RULE: emphasis from WEIGHT + COLOR, never SIZE — run a near-uniform type size and carry meaning with a bolder weight (Public Sans 800 on one word) + the ultramarine spike; never solve hierarchy by scaling up. Hold content in a wide LEFT column (max-width ~88%) with a large empty margin, flush-left. Use exactly ONE hairline rule (1px) as the only ornament. Furniture: a small MONOSPACE rail top-left ('FIELD NOTES · 2026') and a mono slide-label bottom-right, constant on every slide. Type: a clean grotesque (Public Sans; Inter/Helvetica Neue fallback) for headline + agenda at a calm size with selective weight; shift the CLOSER to PLAYFAIR DISPLAY serif for one human line. Build three layouts: a COVER (mono rail + short hairline + weight-emphasis headline), a NUMBERED AGENDA (01-04 tabular-nums ultramarine, hairline-separated rows), and a PLAYFAIR closer line with the italic ultramarine spike over a mono cite. Invent generic copy; never a real template brand."
  },
  "layout_and_structure": {
    "description": "A 16:9 deck of three repeatable layouts on a cool-paper ground, unified by a monospace rail top-left, a mono slide-label bottom-right, and one ultramarine spike. Content is always held in a wide left column with a large empty margin. COVER: the rail, a short hairline rule, then a headline anchored low-left where one word is bold + ultramarine. NUMBERED AGENDA: the rail, then 01-04 rows each separated by a 1px hairline, numbers in tabular-nums ultramarine, items in bold ink. CLOSER: the rail, a single Playfair Display serif line with an italic ultramarine spike, and a monospace cite beneath. The rail position, the wide margin, and the weight-not-size rule stay constant so the system reads as one considered deck.",
    "prompts": [
      {
        "part": "Ground, wide margin, and constant furniture",
        "prompt": "Fill every slide with cool paper #e9ecee. Hold all content in a wide LEFT column (max-width ~88%), flush-left, leaving a large empty right/bottom margin. Pin a small MONOSPACE rail top-left ('FIELD NOTES · 2026', ~35px, .1em tracking, uppercase, muted grey) and a small mono slide-label bottom-right at ~50% opacity — both constant on every slide. No boxes, no color blocks, no shadows."
      },
      {
        "part": "Cover — weight-and-color emphasis, not size",
        "prompt": "On the cover, draw a short HAIRLINE RULE (1px, ink, ~36% width) as the only ornament, then anchor a headline low-left in a clean grotesque (Public Sans; Inter/Helvetica Neue fallback) at a calm ~160px, line-height ~1.02. Emphasis comes from WEIGHT + COLOR: run the sentence at a medium weight (~600) and make ONE word bold (~800) AND ultramarine #1c39c4 ('Designing for calm, at scale.'). Never make a word bigger to emphasize it — heavier and blue only."
      },
      {
        "part": "Numbered agenda — structure from hairlines",
        "prompt": "Build the agenda as 01-04 rows, each row separated by a 1px HAIRLINE rule (top and bottom on the set), no boxes. Numbers in monospace tabular-nums, ultramarine #1c39c4; items in bold ink at a calm size (~64px). The hairlines and the numbered rhythm carry the structure — add no color fills or icons."
      },
      {
        "part": "Closer — the Playfair register shift",
        "prompt": "For the closer, shift register to PLAYFAIR DISPLAY (serif): one line held in the left column (~105px, line-height ~1.18) with the emphasized clause in italic bold ultramarine ('The work isn't louder. It's quieter, on purpose.'), then a monospace cite beneath in muted grey. This single serif slide is the one human note in an otherwise grotesque deck — use it only to close."
      }
    ]
  },
  "special_ui_components": [
    {
      "component": "Weight-and-color emphasis (never size)",
      "description": "The governing device: hierarchy carried by a bolder weight + a single ultramarine spike, at one calm type size.",
      "prompt": "Run the deck at a near-uniform type size and carry all emphasis with WEIGHT + COLOR: keep the base at a medium weight and make the emphasized word heavier (e.g. Public Sans 800) AND ultramarine #1c39c4. Never scale a word up to emphasize it. This restraint is the whole Swiss personality — one size, selective weight, one accent."
    },
    {
      "component": "Single ultramarine spike",
      "description": "One ultramarine #1c39c4 used only as a spike — a few words, agenda numbers, the italic closer word — never a fill.",
      "prompt": "Use ultramarine #1c39c4 as the ONLY accent, and only as a SPIKE: one emphasized word per headline, the agenda numbers, the italic closer clause. Never fill a shape or a background with it. On cool paper + near-black ink, the spike is the single point of energy the eye lands on."
    },
    {
      "component": "Hairline-only ornament + wide margin",
      "description": "A single 1px hairline rule as the deck's only ornament, with content held in a wide left column against large negative space.",
      "prompt": "Allow exactly ONE hairline rule (1px, ink) as ornament — a short rule under the cover title, and the row dividers in the agenda. No boxes, shadows, gradients, or icons. Hold all content flush-left in a wide left column (max-width ~88%) with a large empty right/bottom margin; the negative space is a design element, not leftover room."
    },
    {
      "component": "Playfair closer (register shift)",
      "description": "A single serif closing line (Playfair Display) with an italic ultramarine spike — the one human note in a grotesque deck.",
      "prompt": "Close on ONE Playfair Display serif line held in the left column, with the emphasized clause in italic bold ultramarine, over a monospace cite. This is the only serif and the only register shift in the deck — use it strictly to close, so the shift stays meaningful and the body stays quietly grotesque throughout."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "An EDITORIAL MAGAZINE PITCH-DECK SYSTEM at 16:9 (1600x900 slides), designed as a set of REPEATABLE layouts that read as one magazine, not three unrelated templates. GROUND: off-white / warm cream #f1ece1 on content slides, with a subtle FILM-GRAIN overlay (~6% opacity, SVG feTurbulence) on every slide for a printed-paper feel. COLOR: strictly off-white + near-black ink #1c1913 + ONE brick-red accent #b3401f (a slightly warmer #a2451f is acceptable for the small furniture caps). No second color, no photos, no gradient decoration. TYPE SYSTEM: the hero is ANTON (a tall CONDENSED grotesque, loaded from Google Fonts; fall back to Oswald / Archivo Narrow / Bebas Neue, NEVER a normal-width sans) set ALL-CAPS in brick-red at massive scale (~340-360px on the cover) with tight leading (line-height ~.8) so a 1-2 word stack fills the lower two-thirds; body/editorial lines are a clean sans (Public Sans) in a muted ink; the SECTION BREAK shifts register to PLAYFAIR DISPLAY serif. FURNITURE (the through-line): tracked ALL-CAPS labels (~.2em tracking, weight 700, brick-red) pinned to the TOP margin — a wordmark/section label at top-left and a year or slide-number at top-right — REPEAT in the same position on every content slide; a mono slide-label sits bottom-right. THREE LAYOUTS: (1) COVER = top furniture + one enormous Anton word-stack anchored to the bottom + a tracked-caps byline on the baseline; (2) CONTENT/STAT = same top furniture + a giant Anton number/stat + a short editorial sentence beneath at ~50px in muted ink (max-width ~70%); (3) SECTION BREAK = invert to a SOLID brick-red ground with cream text, a small Anton section number top-left, and a large Playfair Display serif headline centered — the one slide that changes register so the deck breathes. Invent generic copy (e.g. 'SHIP / WEEKLY', 'R3XDEC DESIGN · 2026') — never a template brand.",
  "style": {
    "description": "Editorial magazine-cover-as-slide: the type IS the image and the FURNITURE is the brand. A warm off-white #f1ece1 ground under a faint film-grain gives a printed-paper feel; the whole deck is off-white + near-black ink + ONE brick-red accent, no photos and no second color. The signature is one enormous tall-CONDENSED grotesque (Anton) set all-caps in brick-red at poster scale with tight leading, so a one- or two-word hero fills most of the slide. Tracked all-caps labels pinned to the top corners repeat on every slide and are what make the set read as one designed magazine. A single Playfair Display section break, on an inverted solid brick-red ground, is the deliberate register shift that keeps a condensed-sans deck from feeling monotone. Loud, editorial, restrained to one accent, and coherent because the furniture never moves.",
    "prompt": "Design an EDITORIAL MAGAZINE PITCH-DECK SYSTEM at 16:9 as repeatable layouts, not one slide. Ground: warm off-white #f1ece1 with a faint film-grain overlay (~6%, SVG feTurbulence) on every slide. Color: off-white + near-black ink #1c1913 + ONE brick-red accent #b3401f only — no photos, no second color, no gradient decoration. Hero type: Anton (tall CONDENSED grotesque, Oswald/Archivo-Narrow/Bebas fallback, never a normal-width sans), ALL CAPS, brick-red, ~340-360px on the cover with line-height ~.8 so a 1-2 word stack fills the lower two-thirds. Furniture: tracked all-caps labels (weight 700, ~.2em, brick-red) pinned top-left (wordmark) and top-right (year/number), REPEATING in the same spot on every content slide, plus a mono slide-label bottom-right. Build three layouts: a COVER (furniture + giant word-stack + tracked-caps byline on the baseline), a CONTENT/STAT slide (furniture + giant Anton number + one short editorial sentence in muted ink), and a SECTION BREAK that inverts to a solid brick-red ground with cream text and a large Playfair Display serif headline. Invent generic copy; never a real template brand."
  },
  "layout_and_structure": {
    "description": "A 16:9 deck of three repeatable layouts sharing one grid: a top-margin furniture row (label left / year or number right) and a mono slide-label bottom-right on every slide. COVER: furniture on top, one enormous Anton all-caps word-stack anchored to the bottom, a tracked-caps byline on the baseline. CONTENT/STAT: same furniture, a giant Anton number/stat, and a short editorial sentence beneath in muted ink (max-width ~70%). SECTION BREAK: the palette inverts to a solid brick-red ground with cream text, a small Anton section number top-left, and a large Playfair Display serif headline centered. The furniture position is constant across all slides so the system reads as one magazine.",
    "prompts": [
      {
        "part": "Ground, grain, and repeating furniture",
        "prompt": "Fill each slide with warm off-white #f1ece1 and lay a faint film-grain overlay (~6% opacity, SVG feTurbulence fractalNoise) over it. Pin a tracked ALL-CAPS furniture row to the TOP margin on every content slide: a wordmark/section label at top-left and a year or slide-number at top-right, both weight 700, ~.2em tracking, brick-red #b3401f (or the warmer #a2451f). Add a small monospace slide-label ('01 / cover') bottom-right at ~50% opacity. This furniture is the through-line — keep its position identical on every slide."
      },
      {
        "part": "Cover — one enormous Anton word-stack",
        "prompt": "On the cover, set a 1-2 word hero in Anton (tall CONDENSED grotesque; Oswald/Archivo-Narrow/Bebas fallback, never a normal-width sans), ALL CAPS, brick-red #b3401f, ~340-360px with line-height ~.8, left-aligned and anchored to the bottom so the stack fills the lower two-thirds ('SHIP / WEEKLY'). Beneath it on the baseline, a tracked ALL-CAPS byline in near-black ink ('PRESENTED BY J. ZHOU · Q3 REVIEW')."
      },
      {
        "part": "Content / stat slide",
        "prompt": "Keep the top furniture, then center a giant Anton stat/number in brick-red at large scale (a huge '3.4x' feel, line-height ~.78), with a single short editorial sentence beneath in a clean muted-ink sans (Public Sans) at ~50px, max-width ~70%. One idea per slide; the number carries the slide."
      },
      {
        "part": "Section break — the register shift",
        "prompt": "For a section break, INVERT the palette: a solid brick-red #b3401f ground with cream #f1ece1 text. Put a small Anton section number top-left, and center a large PLAYFAIR DISPLAY serif headline (weight 700, line-height ~.98). This is the one slide that changes typeface and ground, so it lets a condensed-sans deck breathe — use it sparingly (section dividers only)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "special_ui_components": [
    {
      "component": "Enormous Anton condensed word-stack (cover hero)",
      "description": "One or two all-caps words in a tall condensed grotesque, brick-red, packed tight so the type fills the slide.",
      "prompt": "Set a 1-2 word hero in Anton (tall CONDENSED grotesque; Oswald/Archivo-Narrow/Bebas fallback, never a normal-width sans), ALL CAPS, brick-red #b3401f, ~340-360px with line-height ~.8, left-aligned and bottom-anchored so it fills the lower two-thirds. The condensed width is the look — protect it through any font substitution; a normal-width sans leaves gaps and kills it."
    },
    {
      "component": "Repeating tracked-caps editorial furniture",
      "description": "The top-margin label/year row (plus a mono slide-label) that repeats in the same position on every slide and makes the deck read as one magazine.",
      "prompt": "Pin a tracked ALL-CAPS row to the top margin on every slide: a wordmark/section label top-left, a year or slide-number top-right, weight 700, ~.2em tracking, brick-red. Add a small monospace slide-label bottom-right at ~50% opacity. Never move these positions between slides — the constant furniture is the system's through-line."
    },
    {
      "component": "Playfair section break (register shift)",
      "description": "An inverted solid brick-red slide with a Playfair Display serif headline — the deliberate change of typeface and ground that punctuates the deck.",
      "prompt": "Build a section-divider slide that inverts to a solid brick-red #b3401f ground with cream text, a small Anton section number top-left, and a large Playfair Display serif headline (weight 700) centered. Use it only for section transitions so the shift stays meaningful and the condensed-sans body never feels monotone."
    },
    {
      "component": "Single-accent + film-grain discipline",
      "description": "Off-white ground + near-black ink + ONE brick-red accent, unified by a faint grain overlay on every slide.",
      "prompt": "Constrain the whole deck to off-white #f1ece1 + near-black ink #1c1913 + ONE brick-red accent #b3401f. No photos, no second color, no gradient decoration. Lay a faint film-grain overlay (~6%, SVG feTurbulence) over every slide so the deck reads as printed paper and all layouts share one surface."
    }
  ]
}
